  "claim": "borg_new_kill() read the race of the reused tracking slot before storing the new race, so its final floor/wall step used an empty race and marked every newly seen monster's grid as floor. A pass-wall monster first seen inside rock thus turned the rock into floor in the Borg's map, defeating the 'never shoot walls' check: a level-1 Warrior fired a sling shot at an earth spirit inside a granite pillar, losing the turn and the shot for 0 damage. borg_update_kill_old(), called just before, already does that step with the right race; removing the stale duplicate keeps the wall and the shot is not taken. The open-floor control (shot hits for 4) is byte-identical.",
